WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.235
Even the White House says

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.570
it does not know the current

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.671
whereabouts of the man

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.106
who led last week's short

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.741
lived rebellion in Russia

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.110
and Ukraine's military intelligence chief

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.045
says that Russia's FSB,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.214
the successor agency to the KGB,

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.516
is plotting to kill Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.618
quoting him now from an interview.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:18.818
Quote,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.321
We are aware that the FSB was charged

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.390
for the task to assassinate him.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.492
Will they be successful in doing that?

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.327
We'll see what time.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:27.660
We're joined

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.995
now by CNN national security

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:29.863
analyst Steve Hall,

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.332
a former CIA chief of Russia operations.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.100
Steve, I mean,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.368
how likely is it

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.870
that the FSB knows

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.872
exactly where Prigozhin is

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.473
and if they wanted to kill him?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.376
How hard would it be for them to do it?

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.712
Yeah, I would say that

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.680
this analytical statement by the

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.948
by the Ukrainian military

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.217
intelligence is not a huge stretch.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.453
It's not it's not a particularly bad

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.421
analytical position.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.321
If I were a betting man,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.156
I think, for

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.558
instance, significant trouble,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.125
you know,

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.428
threats from the FSB to begin with.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.063
You know, the FSB is extremely good.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.130
They'll be able to find him.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.231
They know how to kill people.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.067
We've seen that many times before.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.402
For me, the big question is, why now?

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:10.103
I mean this.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.371
If they were going to kill them,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.172
the time to have done

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:12.906
it would have been

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.773
before he caused

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.741
all of the difficulties

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:15.575
that he has caused.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.610
And of course, the FSB is the

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.978
are the ones who are responsible.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.214
It's the organization that is responsible

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.682
for informing the president

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.550
in this case, Putin

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.717
and those close to him

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.885
that something is amiss.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.420
And either they did that

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.655
and he ignored it

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.524
unlikely or they failed to to see it.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.960
And so yeah, it's kind of obvious

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.627
now that they would want

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:35.195
to get rid of them.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.996
But why not two or three weeks ago,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.298
they would have saved themselves

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.566
a lot of trouble had they done it.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.233
That what's

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.668
keeping Prigozhin alive,

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:42.669
if he is still alive,

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.337
we haven't seen the guy.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.605
Yeah. This is another thing.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.240
Is this that we just don't know?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.440
You know,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.142
what's good is so little information

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.509
right now.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.710
And of course, this is what the Russian

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.211
one of the things

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.112
the Russians are really good

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.646
at is putting question marks

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:54.681
above these guys.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.249
So percussion, you know,

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.517
the rumor is well,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.786
everybody's saying that he's you know

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.187
you know, happy and healthy.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.155
Maybe not so happy,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.690
but he's in Belarus someplace.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.757
Thanks to the intervention

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.826
of President Lukashenko,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.962
we haven't seen the sort of weekend

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:09.529
either.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.363
Another guy who

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.998
there's a lot of question marks over.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.833
In a sense, though, this plays

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.235
into what I think

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.270
the Kremlin is trying to do, which is,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.606
you know, if they do the expected it,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.474
they go ahead and kill these guys.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.308
Then everybody's like,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.376
okay, well, that's predictable.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.277
And now that's over.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.044
And we're past that

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.147
by keeping some questions out there.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.615
I think it keeps people

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:31.518
that Putin is still unsure about on edge

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.619
and perhaps

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.620
they will make a mistake,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.921
which will then put them on the list

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.556
to be gotten rid of the well as well.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.991
So there's some housekeeping that needs.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.124
Yeah,

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.192
I was just going to ask

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.227
about keeping his internal house

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.163
in order.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.031
Who are the people that Putin

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.833
is most concerned about now?

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.037
It's hard to say because of

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:51.704
the nature

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.573
of how difficult it is to predict

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.974
what's going on inside the Kremlin.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.243
I think we all probably remember the days

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.678
when we were looking at

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.613
how many guys were on top of Lenin's tomb

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.648
when people were marching by.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.582
And that gave us an idea

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.050
as to what was going on.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.652
It's still very, very hard to know

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.053
what's going on inside the Kremlin.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.188
But obviously the people

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.455
who have the most power

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.757
and who are closest to Putin

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.992
are the ones who ironically

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.194
are not only the ones

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.094
who would be called upon

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.162
to take care of problems,

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:16.829
but also the ones

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.331
who pose the greatest danger.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.966
So the head of the FSB,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.901
the head of the other security services,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.703
even the senior military guys,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.371
I think are at risk.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.340
And yeah, he's got to do something

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.474
whether Putin does

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.976
whether or not it's a Stalin

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.477
like purge of everybody

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.546
or whether it's something more modulated

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.848
than that. We'll just have to see.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.651
It is fascinating how history sometimes

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.786
seems to repeat itself.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.321
Steve Hall, great to have you here.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.690
I suspect we'll be talking soon

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.259
about some of this. I bet so.

